course: dictionary
lesson: 1525
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A century is a period of one hundred years. That is its main meaning, and it is used in maths and history. Two centuries is 200 years, and half a century is 50 years.
explain: History uses centuries to say when things happened. Years in the 1900s belong to the 20th century, so the context of a date tells you the century. Each century has its own number, and you can check it by counting from year 1.
explain: Cricket has a different meaning. When one batter scores one hundred runs, they have made a century. It is the same word, but now it is about runs, not years. Look at the words around it to decide which meaning is being used.
fact: A century is a period of one hundred years.
fact: «Someone born in 1989 was born in the 1900s, the 20th century.»
fact: The 1st century was years 1 to 100, and the 21st century runs from 2001 to 2100.
fact: «For centuries» means for a very long time, as in «people in Ukrainian lands called themselves Rusyny for centuries».
fact: In cricket, a century is one hundred runs scored by one player.
exercise: How many years are there in half a century? | 10 | *50 | 5 | 500
exercise: A batter in cricket scores one hundred runs. What have they made? | *A century | A duck | A maiden over | A boundary
exercise: Someone was born in 1989. Which century were they born in? | The 19th century | *The 20th century | The 18th century | The 21st century
test: How many years are there in two centuries? | 2 | 20 | 2000 | *200
test: «People in Ukrainian lands called themselves Rusyny for centuries.» What does for centuries mean? | For a short while | For one day | *For a very long time | For exactly one year
exam: Which century were the years 1 to 100 in? | The 0th century | *The 1st century | The 100th century | The 10th century
